fof_version: '0.1'
type: enemy
id: kindly_one
name: A Kindly One
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 0.1.0
enemy:
  tier: named
  attack_modifier: 0
  defense_modifier: 3
  armor: none
  techniques:
  - fair_offer
  - the_unforgiven_slight
  special: 'FAIR OFFER — a Kindly One cannot decline a genuinely fair trade, and
    knows fair from unfair without being told. No roll. The MM does not get to refuse
    on its behalf.

    THE UNFORGIVEN SLIGHT — a Kindly One cheated once never trades with that person
    again, nor does any other. There is no roll for this either, and no apology
    that works.'
  description: Waist-high, dressed in whatever it has most recently been given,
    and holding something out. The Kindly are always holding something out. They
    speak politely, in whatever language you used first, and they will wait a very
    long time for an answer.
  disposition: Does not fight. Has never fought. Will absolutely stand there while
    you decide whether you are going to.
  first_target: None. If struck, a Kindly One defends itself by being extremely
    difficult to hit and by leaving.
  triggers:
  - Opens every encounter with an offer, and the offer is always real.
  - Never lies, never haggles twice, and never mentions the slight again — to you.
  morale: Leaves at the first Condition, and does not come back. Neither does any
    other Kindly One, anywhere, for the rest of the campaign.
  organization: Alone, at a crossing, a threshold, or a place where something was
    lost.
  notes: 'TR breakdown: offense(+0 → 2) + durability(Resolve 4) + armor(none → 0)
    + techniques(2) = 8. The number exists so a table that starts a fight has one
    to finish. It is not an invitation.'
  negotiation: Wants a fair trade, and defines fair generously. Shifts for anything
    genuinely valued by its owner rather than anything expensive. Honours every
    bargain to the letter, including the ones you would rather it read loosely.
  resolve: 4
created_at: '2026-08-02T00:00:00+00:00'
last_modified: '2026-08-02T00:00:00+00:00'
